# smoke-multi.list — smoke scenarios that need a second monitor.
#
# Added to the live smoke (`ADRT_SESSION_SMOKE=1`) only when the session has more
# than one monitor connected, so a one-screen laptop run stays short while a
# docked/multi-screen run also exercises the multi-monitor behaviour. Entries
# self-skip when the hardware is not there, so this is safe to include only when
# it applies. Same rules as smoke.list: one id per line, `#` comments, and an
# entry with no scenario file aborts the run by name.
#
#   multi-monitor tiling, non-primary tileable, move across screens without a
#   stale classification, and the other screen surviving a workspace switch
#                                        S15-multi-monitor
#   every connected screen keeps its own axis and contains its windows, for any
#   number of mixed-orientation screens and arrangement
#                                        S25-screen-topology

S15-multi-monitor
S25-screen-topology
